      "message": "fix(post): G76 words state the thread passes that were verified\n\nWith the G76Cycle post option the control cuts the passes itself, so\nthe thread-cycle record now states exactly the passes the kernel laid\nand the verdict judged, in the cycle's own terms: first depth dd, the\nminimum dmin (the rung for constant depth, which the control's clamp\nturns into equal steps), the finishing pass's own depth d, m - 1\nspring passes, tool angle a = 2 x flank angle, and a flank record\nstarting at the crest's flank station.\n\nGolden change, on purpose: thread_g76.nc goes from\n`G76 P010000 Q400 R0` to `G76 P010000 Q400 R0.4`. With R0 the control\nroughs 0.4, 0.8, 1.2 and then cuts its finishing pass at the root a\nsecond time - a fourth pass at full depth the verdict never judged\n(not a gouge, the same root, but not what was verified). R0.4 is the\nfinishing pass's own depth, so the control roughs 0.4, 0.8 and\nfinishes at 1.2: the three passes verified. The G32 output and the\nlaid passes are unchanged. (The #363 research read the mismatch as a\ndecreasing ladder; dmin = infeed already clamped every step to the\nrung, so the roughing matched - the extra root pass was the gap.)\n\nRefused by name with G76 chosen: alternating flank infeed (new\n`alternating` flag on the record, `ALT 1` in the stream only when set,\nan optional project cache key), a flank angle whose double is not a\nG76 tool angle, and a one-pass thread. lathe_post_g76_schedule models\nthe control's schedule from the posted words and pins it equal to\nthe laid depths and stations (golden thread_g76_area.nc).\n\nFixes #417\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
